# Mobile Production Environment

Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values before building for production.

```env
# Backend API — must be HTTPS in production
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.nova.leadup.tech

# Optional: override if your backend runs on a non-standard port
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_PORT=
```

## Android Signing

Set these environment variables in your CI secrets or local shell before running
`./gradlew assembleRelease`:

```bash
export ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PATH=/path/to/keystore.jks
export ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=<keystore-password>
export ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS=<key-alias>
export ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD=<key-password>
```

Alternatively, place a `keystore.properties` file next to the `android/` directory
(do NOT commit it — it is git-ignored):

```properties
storeFile=/path/to/keystore.jks
storePassword=<keystore-password>
keyAlias=<key-alias>
keyPassword=<key-password>
```

To generate a new keystore:

```bash
keytool -genkeypair -v \
  -keystore nova-release.jks \
  -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 \
  -alias nova \
  -storepass <password> \
  -keypass <password> \
  -dname "CN=NOVA, O=Leadup Technologies, L=City, ST=State, C=US"
```

Keep the keystore file and password safe — losing them means you cannot update
the app on the Play Store.
